  "description": "I need to get married. But men aren't exactly lining up to meet me, and there aren't many prospects in this small town. \n\nActually, there is one.\nMy childhood friend, Cha I-hyeok.\nHe whispers in my ear in a devilish tone. \n\n“I guess you don't have a choice, you'll have to marry me.”\nIs he a man? Sure. He's a good-looking guy, but we're like family. \n\n“Are you crazy? No. I can't marry you.”\n“Why not?”\n“If we get married, we'll have to do... things at night. How can we do that with you and me?”\n“Well, we can try it out.”\n“Try what?”\n“Kiss… or have sex.” \n\nBefore I could scold him for his insanity, I-hyeok kisses my lips roughly.\nThe moist, hot feeling is unfamiliar.\nHis lips, nibbling on mine, swells slightly.\nAnd it's not just his lips that's swelling. I can feel him get hard, pressing against my flesh. \n\n“Huh....”\nWe are friends.\nNo…\nWe were friends.\nFriends don't kiss like this. \n\nWhat are we now, then? \n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
